  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on NRS_484B_407: 10 witnesses, all with their planned names, and no compositions. I used 3 of the 6 gate runs, but the first two were mistakes. I triggered them on the unedited skeleton when I meant to read a Core file, and both returned `UNUSED_CLAIM` as expected. Two other shell calls also broke the one-command rule: a directory listing of Core ran, and a `--help` probe of the gate was denied. None of these changed a file. All of this is recorded in `task_result.md`.\n\n**Rule** (`TrafficSpec.Rules.NRS_484B_407`):\n- **Class:** the subject belongs to the aggregate `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`.\n- **Under way:** the subject's yaw rate magnitude is above `p.turn_yaw_rate_tol`.\n- **Condition:** (s3 or s4) and s5:\n  - s3: the subject occupies a roadway whose curvature is above `p.curvature_resolution`.\n  - s4: a crest is within `p.crest_near_reach` of the subject's body.\n  - s5: the roadway the subject occupies has a sight distance below 500 ft.\n- **Applicability:** read as the plan's \"some moment\" over the turn window. Some single observation in the `p.vehicle_turn_window` behind must show the turn under way and the whole condition holding together.\n- **Obligation:** `drv_motion_u_turn` does not hold.\n- **No narrowings declared.** s5's \"at its place\" is read as the roadway region the subject occupies, because sight distance belongs to a region. This uses only names the node already claims.\n\n**Witnesses:** every scenario uses one 23-second trace with a 180° reversal recognized at t = 18 s, and is judged over t = 11–22 s so no look-back window is cut off at the trace start.\n- **permit:** the subject follows the bend at 6 °/s. That engages the rule without any reversal, so the result is compliant rather than not applicable.\n- **occasion_s3:** a U-turn curls back toward its start, so it can't move steadily along the road. Only the middle of the turn (t = 13–15 s) lies on the bend, not strictly its \"second half\" as the narrative says. The turn still begins on the straight, which is what this scenario tests.\n\nFiles are in `library/TrafficSpec`:\n- `Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_407.lean`\n- `TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_407.lean`\n- `results/full221-1116-1018/iter-002/code/NRS_484B_407/task_result.md`",
